1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Orion: Three Stars the Whole World Knows
/ China: Shen. Egypt: Sah. The
Kamilaroi: Birray Birray.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:10,000
China calls them Shen (“three”). Egypt:
Sah. Australia’s Kamilaroi: Birray
Birray.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Orion’s Belt: three similarly bright
stars in a straight line, under 3°
across.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Almost on the celestial equator, they
rise due east — from the Arctic to New
Zealand.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The Kamilaroi: the Belt is Birray
Birray, three young boys. Rigel is their
campfire, the Sword their fire stick.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The Maya: creation’s fire. Three stars
form a triangle of hearthstones. The
Orion Nebula is its smoke.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The Aztecs saw a wooden fire drill.
Every 52 years, all fires were put out.
Priests drilled a new one on a hilltop.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
If no fire caught, the Aztecs believed
the sun would not rise again.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Look southeast: red Betelgeuse top left,
blue-white Rigel bottom right, the Belt
in between. Brightest below: Sirius.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Hawaiʻi: Four Star Lines Home. 1976: no
compass, no map — 34 days to Tahiti.

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

